  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AJ9">Lemma <span data-tag="0AJ9">87.17.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a formal algebraic space over $S$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the reduction of $X$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0AIN" data-tag="0AIN">87.12.1</a>) is a quasi-compact algebraic space, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
we can find $\{ X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ as in Definition <a href="/tag/0AIM" data-tag="0AIM">87.11.1</a> with $I$ finite, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a morphism $Y \to X$ representable by algebraic spaces which is étale and surjective and where $Y$ is an affine formal algebraic space. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
